  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...A strong system Friday through Saturday is \nexpected to bring widespread rain with some snow over the North \nFriday/Friday night and strong winds Friday night into Saturday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nA strong low pressure system is expected to develop over the \nGreat Lakes, then move east towards the state this weekend. This\nsystem is expected to bring widespread precip to the region \nFriday. As of this update, ensemble solutions are gradually \nconverging on a track through the center of the state but there \nare still groupings of members wanting to take the track north \nand south of the area. The track through the area is relatively \nfavorable for some snowfall in northern areas as winds will have\nan easterly component, preventing substantial warm air from \nadvecting into the area. Most areas that see snow will probably \nsee less than an inch but a few areas near the canadian border \nmight reach an inch or possibly two. Snow amounts are likely to \nbe terrain dependent with higher elevations receiving the \ngreater amounts. Some slick roads possible Friday night as \ntemperatures drop to around freezing. Snow showers are likely to\npersist into Saturday with strong, gusty winds up to 40 mph. \nAlong with temperatures in the 30s this is likely to result in \nwind chills dipping into the 20s. Isolated power outages are\npossible.",
